      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BAD GIRL RIVER (1) was safely held in tougher company last start after drifting back at this track, but prior to that won by 1.3 lengths at this track (17.80) beating Flying Blue Moon in a Grade 5 on August 26. Some good form is emerging from her last run. Should be very hard to beat this time. MISS MULWEE (6) made light work of a wide draw last time with a slick early sectional but gathered in and had to settle for the minors, finishing third (22.79) at Gosford over 388m. Expected to be in the finish again. NATURE BOY (2) was well backed last start but ran below expectations when fifth (22.91), beaten 9 lengths. Was in the money the start prior. Remains without a win from the draw but has been in the placings two times from four attempts. Has ability and is one of the better chances.",
